<section>
  <h2>Wedding security for one function or several days</h2>
  <p>Planning a wedding, reception, engagement, haldi, mehendi or sangeet? Ask our Barasat branch about temporary gate guards, darwan and bouncers. Request 1, 2, 3, 4 or a few days of cover with a separate schedule for each venue and function.</p>
  <p>Local venue corridors include Barasat–Barrackpore Road, Jessore Road through Madhyamgram, Sodepur Road, the Barrackpore side and Rajarhat–New Town. We also accept wider enquiries within approximately 50 km, subject to the exact entrance, access rules and available staff.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Agree the wedding guard posts</h2>
  <ul><li><strong>Gate darwan:</strong> follow the host's guest-list and invitation arrangements at agreed entrances.</li><li><strong>Bouncers:</strong> manage busy entry periods and restricted access with calm communication and de-escalation.</li><li><strong>Family and vendor access:</strong> identify family-only rooms, service entrances and supplier reporting points.</li><li><strong>Venue vehicle entry:</strong> coordinate the venue's agreed drop-off and parking approach with its staff.</li><li><strong>Late or overnight duties:</strong> book separate shifts for late departures, setup or pack-down where required.</li></ul>
  <p>For a hall-and-lawn property, confirm which space is in use and whether the hall, lawn and service gate need separate posts. Families using more than one venue should share the movement schedule rather than just the wedding date.</p>
</section>
<section>
  <h2>Venue planning around Barasat and Kolkata</h2>
  <p>Our <a href="/services/banquet-event-security-barasat-kolkata/">map-linked hall, lawn and ground guide</a> includes references around Nabapally, Madhyamgram, Barrackpore, New Town and outer enquiry areas. References are landmarks, not venue partnerships or booking availability.</p>
  <p>Obtain the venue's agreement to outside security and send its actual entrance pin. The written quote should confirm staff type, count, hours, travel and any extra-hours terms. Catering, decoration, valet driving and wedding planning are separate from the security brief.</p>
</section>
